  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "The 454545-th FIDE Chess Olympiad is currently being held in Budapest, Hungary.\n\nEvery round, teams of four players each face off against each other in four individual games.\n\nA team receives 111 point for winning a game, 0.50.50.5 points for a draw, and 000 points for a loss.\n\nA team is said to win the round if they receive **strictly** more points than the opposing team.\n\nIn the current round, your favorite team has already won XXX games, drawn YYY games, and lost ZZZ games.\n\nCan they still win this round?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input will contain three space-separated integers X,Y,X, Y, X,Y, and ZZZ — the number of wins, draws, and losses so far.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint a single string: either `\"YES\"` or `\"NO\"` (without quotes), denoting whether your team can still win the round.\n\n\nEach character of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e, the strings `NO`, `No`, `nO`, and `no` will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "0≤X,Y,Z≤40 \\leq X, Y, Z \\leq 40≤X,Y,Z≤4",
      "X+Y+Z≤4X+Y+Z \\leq 4X+Y+Z≤4"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 1 0",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nWith one game won and one drawn, the team has 1+0.5=1.51+0.5 = 1.51+0.5=1.5 points already, while their opponent has 0+0.5=0.50 + 0.5 = 0.50+0.5=0.5.\nThere are two games remaining - if they win both, they will receive another two points while their opponent receives 000, making the final scoreline 3.53.53.5 to 0.50.50.5 and hence a team victory."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 0 2",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nWith two wins and two losses, both teams are on 222 points.\nThere are no games remaining, so it's not possible for us to have strictly more points than the opposition."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "0 1 1",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nWith one draw and one loss, we have 0.50.50.5 points while the opponent has 1.51.51.5.\nHowever, if our team wins both remaining games, they'll end up on 2.52.52.5 points while the opponent will stay on 1.51.51.5, and hence our team wins the round."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_4",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "0 2 1",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nWe have 0.5+0.5=10.5 + 0.5 = 10.5+0.5=1 point, while the opponent has 0.5+0.5+1=20.5 + 0.5 + 1 = 20.5+0.5+1=2 points.\nThere is one game left, even if we win it and receive 111 point, the score will be 222 points each.\nSince our score is not strictly greater than the opponent's score, we can't win the round."
      }
    ]
  },
